From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Answer a token request with no user instead of asserting

GetToken() checks IsSignedIn() and calls RequestToken(), which asserts
IsSignedIn() again.  A sign-out on another thread can land between the two:
SignOut() clears the user without the provider's mutex, and the token
generation moves only once its notification reaches OnAuthStateChanged().
The assertion throws and the process aborts.

Answer the request as GetToken() does when nobody is signed in.  A sign-out
after this check gets a failed token future from Auth, which OnToken()
already passes on as an error.
---
 firestore/src/main/credentials_provider_desktop.cc | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/firestore/src/main/credentials_provider_desktop.cc b/firestore/src/main/credentials_provider_desktop.cc
index 8182c34..5da7c98 100644
--- a/firestore/src/main/credentials_provider_desktop.cc
+++ b/firestore/src/main/credentials_provider_desktop.cc
@@ -222,8 +222,14 @@ void FirebaseCppCredentialsProvider::OnAuthStateChanged(void* context) {
 
 void FirebaseCppCredentialsProvider::RequestToken(
     TokenListener<AuthToken> listener) {
-  SIMPLE_HARD_ASSERT(IsSignedIn(),
-                     "Cannot get token when there is no signed-in user");
+  // GetToken() checked a moment ago, but a sign-out on another thread can
+  // land in between: SignOut() clears the user without this mutex, and the
+  // token generation moves only once its notification reaches
+  // OnAuthStateChanged(). Answer as GetToken() does for no user.
+  if (!IsSignedIn()) {
+    listener(AuthToken::Unauthenticated());
+    return;
+  }
 
   // Take note of the current value of `token_generation` so that this request
   // can fail if there is a token change while the request is outstanding.
-- 
